        "original_id": "42e1f387-b11b-5cb8-b70c-e381238c6779",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charlie Kendall, Donald Sterling, Bobby Samini, V. Stiviano\n- Organizations: Los Angeles Clippers, National Basketball Association, TMZ\n- Topics: ownership interest, litigation, legal representation\n\nFacts:\n- In 1982, Charlie Kendall was reportedly interested in purchasing the Los Angeles Clippers from owner Donald Sterling, but Donald Sterling did not sell the team.\n- Donald Sterling, born Donald Tokowitz on April 26, 1934, is a Jewish-American businessman.\n- Bobby Samini served as lead counsel to former Los Angeles Clippers owner Donald Sterling in highly publicized litigation involving the National Basketball Association, TMZ, and V. Stiviano.",
